  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Collective Plate",
    "overview": "\n**Creative North Star: \"The Collective Plate\"**\n\nOne world, light only, drawn from a printed-poster palette: a full cobalt field, a warm paper \"plate\" ground, hot magenta for the one thing that is done or breaking, and ink for everything that must be read. Everything is hard-edged. There are no radii (except the check circle), no shadows, no gradients except one hard-stop stripe, and no blends: state changes cut over 200 ms, nothing bounces. The look is lifted from a printed manual more than from a software theme, and it reads as a working surface first.\n\nThe system has two voices. The grocery app at `/` holds the world to a working density: fixed rem type, a single 45rem column, 46 px rows. The series figures reuse the same components (Plate, Shelf, ScrubBar, Mark, Band) inside the reader's page. Sync state is drawn with a shared symbol set (plus, circle, hourglass, diamond, stairs, starburst, eye), so a change has a shape from the moment it is made until the server confirms it.\n\nThe condensed display face is rationed: the masthead name, category heads and plate titles only. Red Hat Text does every control and row; Red Hat Mono names ids and devices.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Three working colours (cobalt, plate, ink) with magenta as the accent; lemon is a highlight, not a surface.",
      "Rules, not boxes: 2 px cobalt rules (`--rule`) and 1 px row dividers (`--rule-thin`) do the structuring.",
      "Pointed-end buttons: the one distinctive silhouette in an otherwise rectangular world.",
      "State has a form and a word, never colour alone (hover and drift, half landed, struck, stripes, dashes).",
      "Flat: zero shadows, zero blur, zero gradients apart from the band's hard-stop stripes."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Pairing Rule",
        "body": "On cobalt, text is plate or white, never ink or magenta. On magenta, text is ink. On plate, small error text is error magenta, never magenta. `src/ui/palette.ts` names `tokens.test.ts` as the check that keeps tokens and palette in step and tests these pairings.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ground Rule",
        "body": "The plate keeps a relative luminance above 0.877 so magenta large text holds 3:1.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ration Rule",
        "body": "The condensed face appears only on the masthead name, category heads and plate titles. Controls, rows and prose never use it.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fixed Box Rule",
        "body": "A state change swaps form inside a box that already exists; it never adds or removes height.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hover-Is-Pending Rule",
        "body": "Pending means a symbol hovering clear of its line with a slow drift (`--drift` 2.4s, alternate, 2 px); acked means half landed on the line; a confirmed entry leaves the shelf.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** reach for the tokens in `src/styles/tokens.css` (`--cobalt`, `--space-*`, `--rule`, `--target`) rather than hardcoding a hex or a pixel value.",
      "**Do** give every state a form and a word: hover, half-landed, struck, stripes, dashes, plus the text of the state.",
      "**Do** keep tap targets at `--target` (2.75rem) or larger and rows at `--row-height`.",
      "**Do** keep motion to 200 ms state changes and the slow drift, and honour `prefers-reduced-motion` (the base sheet collapses all durations).",
      "**Do** use the symbol set for mutations: plus (add), circle (check), diamond (edit), hourglass (remove), stairs (reorder)."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use radius, shadow or blur; the check circle is the only round thing.",
      "**Don't** put ink or magenta text on cobalt, or magenta small text on plate.",
      "**Don't** use lemon as text or a thin line.",
      "**Don't** set controls, rows or prose in the condensed display face.",
      "**Don't** let a state change alter a row's or shelf's box size.",
      "**Don't** use colour alone to carry a state."
    ]
  }
}